WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.173
Oh my God what a handsome family!

2
00:00:03.173 --> 00:00:04.006
(woman laughs)

3
00:00:04.006 --> 00:00:05.430
It's true.

4
00:00:05.430 --> 00:00:08.800
And you guys are teaming up for something very important

5
00:00:08.800 --> 00:00:10.870
and meaningful we're very excited and honored

6
00:00:10.870 --> 00:00:13.960
that you're gonna talk about it with us here, thank you.

7
00:00:13.960 --> 00:00:17.370
You're doing an exciting new music therapy initiative called

8
00:00:17.370 --> 00:00:19.760
MS in harmony.

9
00:00:19.760 --> 00:00:22.340
Now, Courtney, you have been living with MS

10
00:00:22.340 --> 00:00:25.780
since you were 23, but you've been dancing so much.

11
00:00:25.780 --> 00:00:30.780
May I ask at what juncture did this impact your ability

12
00:00:31.210 --> 00:00:34.240
and at what juncture did you feel like

13
00:00:34.240 --> 00:00:37.610
this is now something I need to make a mission.

14
00:00:37.610 --> 00:00:41.500
So I was like you said, I was diagnosed when I was 23.

15
00:00:41.500 --> 00:00:45.000 line:15%
And the first thing I asked my doctor was

16
00:00:45.000 --> 00:00:46.500 line:15%
how is this going to affect my dancing?

17
00:00:46.500 --> 00:00:47.650
Am I going to be able to move?

18
00:00:47.650 --> 00:00:49.550
And the first thing she said to me

19
00:00:49.550 --> 00:00:52.600
was the best thing you could do is to keep moving.

20
00:00:52.600 --> 00:00:53.883
You must keep moving.

21
00:00:55.090 --> 00:00:58.044
So that was music to my ears.

22
00:00:58.044 --> 00:00:59.500
(Ben giggles)

23
00:00:59.500 --> 00:01:00.706
Yeah.

24
00:01:00.706 --> 00:01:02.300
(both laugh)

25
00:01:02.300 --> 00:01:05.150
And I, my grandmother had primary progressive

26
00:01:05.150 --> 00:01:06.150
multiple sclerosis.

27
00:01:06.150 --> 00:01:09.110
And I remember calling the MS society.

28
00:01:09.110 --> 00:01:11.630
I worked with them before I was diagnosed with MS

29
00:01:11.630 --> 00:01:13.340
because of my grandma.

30
00:01:13.340 --> 00:01:16.130
And I was like, surprised I have it, how can I get involved?

31
00:01:16.130 --> 00:01:19.630
What can I do? And I don't really think I gave myself

32
00:01:20.880 --> 00:01:25.580
the opportunity to actually digest the fact that I was

33
00:01:25.580 --> 00:01:28.663
just diagnosed with a chronic neurological illness.

34
00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:33.930
And so I found myself such a great team.

35
00:01:33.930 --> 00:01:36.420
I had great people around me

36
00:01:36.420 --> 00:01:40.100
and then I had my second relapse

37
00:01:40.100 --> 00:01:45.100
and I was dancing for Pit bull at the time.

38
00:01:45.240 --> 00:01:48.849
And we were doing, I think it was the divas live awards.

39
00:01:48.849 --> 00:01:51.160
And I woke up that morning

40
00:01:51.160 --> 00:01:54.393
and I totally lost sight in my left eye.

41
00:01:55.430 --> 00:01:58.030
And it's insane because Mr. Three Oh five,

42
00:01:58.030 --> 00:02:01.224
I had my heels on, I had my like these sexy glasses on

43
00:02:01.224 --> 00:02:03.248
(Ben laughs)

44
00:02:03.248 --> 00:02:05.390
and I was like well, I guess I have a right eye.

45
00:02:05.390 --> 00:02:07.423
So the show must go on.

46
00:02:08.330 --> 00:02:12.420
But I feel like getting involved really helps you.

47
00:02:12.420 --> 00:02:13.550
It makes you feel like you're helping

48
00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:16.510
and what could feel like a very helpless situation.

49
00:02:16.510 --> 00:02:19.850
So, you know getting involved with MS in harmony

50
00:02:20.707 --> 00:02:24.870
has really been such a gift to be able to use music

51
00:02:24.870 --> 00:02:29.870
in such a beautiful and positive way to connect the mind

52
00:02:29.910 --> 00:02:31.520
and the body.

53
00:02:31.520 --> 00:02:33.290
And I'm grateful.

54
00:02:33.290 --> 00:02:35.880
Ben, you're such a musical person,

55
00:02:35.880 --> 00:02:40.470
how does this music therapy work? How does it help people?

56
00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:43.240
So MSinharmony.com is where you can head

57
00:02:43.240 --> 00:02:44.730
to learn all about this.

58
00:02:44.730 --> 00:02:46.310
It's these modules, these little lessons

59
00:02:46.310 --> 00:02:48.560
that Courtney and I both participate in along

60
00:02:48.560 --> 00:02:51.000
with music therapist, a licensed music therapist

61
00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.616 line:15%
and it's little games and exercises that helped you

62
00:02:54.616 --> 00:02:56.100 line:15%
to get in touch with your body

63
00:02:56.100 --> 00:02:58.530 line:15%
and to connect your body and mind whether that's you know,

64
00:02:58.530 --> 00:03:03.410
movement breathing, exercises, memory exercises visa-V

65
00:03:03.410 --> 00:03:05.310
creating a tune for a list of things you need

66
00:03:05.310 --> 00:03:08.033
to remember a grocery list or list of names.

67
00:03:08.980 --> 00:03:11.160
And what I really love about it is that as someone

68
00:03:11.160 --> 00:03:13.680
who is a loved one or someone with MS,

69
00:03:13.680 --> 00:03:16.660
and you know, I sometimes feel that it's obviously

70
00:03:16.660 --> 00:03:18.470
a very independent experience in that you know,

71
00:03:18.470 --> 00:03:20.720
Courtney has so much that she needs to face on her own.

72
00:03:20.720 --> 00:03:23.470
And there's so much of the treatment that it's hard

73
00:03:23.470 --> 00:03:25.950
to understand for somebody that isn't going through MS

74
00:03:25.950 --> 00:03:29.600
And so, this particular therapy for MS in harmony

75
00:03:29.600 --> 00:03:32.220
is something that I think is so inclusive of everyone

76
00:03:32.220 --> 00:03:34.180
in the lives of the people that are up against MS.

77
00:03:34.180 --> 00:03:36.970
So it's not only, you know incredibly helpful to the people

78
00:03:36.970 --> 00:03:39.070
who are being treated but also to the caretakers

79
00:03:39.070 --> 00:03:42.030
and the loved ones who can get on board and participate,

80
00:03:42.030 --> 00:03:43.140
participate with their loved ones

81
00:03:43.140 --> 00:03:45.500
and sing along and dance along.

82
00:03:45.500 --> 00:03:48.210
And addition to that, it's not necessarily

83
00:03:48.210 --> 00:03:50.685
for the capital D dancers and capital S singers.

84
00:03:50.685 --> 00:03:51.518
( Courtney chuckles)

85
00:03:51.518 --> 00:03:53.710
It's something that's a very inclusive, very easy program.

86
00:03:53.710 --> 00:03:56.700
That's much more about the mental state

87
00:03:56.700 --> 00:03:59.360
and how powerful music is to change that.

88
00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:02.180
And to put you in touch with your body rather than

89
00:04:02.180 --> 00:04:04.240
singing on key and doing the right steps

90
00:04:04.240 --> 00:04:08.610
This whole thing just sounds like such an incredibly merit

91
00:04:08.610 --> 00:04:10.720
filled thing that you provided for people

92
00:04:10.720 --> 00:04:14.650
and really quickly, Courtney how are you feeling today?

93
00:04:14.650 --> 00:04:17.070
I feel great. I mean, there are days that

94
00:04:17.070 --> 00:04:21.490 line:15%
I forget I have MS and then there are days where, you know,

95
00:04:21.490 --> 00:04:23.960 line:15%
I have to give myself a moment

96
00:04:23.960 --> 00:04:28.960
and just kind of let myself feel what I'm feeling.

97
00:04:29.120 --> 00:04:33.120
You know, it's really easy to feel like

98
00:04:34.120 --> 00:04:36.810 line:15%
you know, I am this super strong person

99
00:04:36.810 --> 00:04:39.500 line:15%
and I, you know I try to be,

100
00:04:39.500 --> 00:04:43.660 line:15%
but I also had to realize that it was really important to,

101
00:04:43.660 --> 00:04:46.640
you know let myself grieve a little bit, you know,

102
00:04:46.640 --> 00:04:49.620
it was accepting this new normal.

103
00:04:49.620 --> 00:04:52.470
And I think it's important to surround yourself

104
00:04:52.470 --> 00:04:53.680
with people that love you.

105
00:04:53.680 --> 00:04:55.260
And realize that they want to help you.

106
00:04:55.260 --> 00:04:56.860
Everything is second to health.

107
00:04:56.860 --> 00:04:58.940
Everything comes into perspective when it

108
00:04:58.940 --> 00:05:00.130
has to do with health.

109
00:05:00.130 --> 00:05:03.960
And that is why I think not only all the circumstances

110
00:05:03.960 --> 00:05:07.920
but the anxiety of our mortality and health right now.

111
00:05:07.920 --> 00:05:11.010
So just thank you for sharing this and for more information

112
00:05:11.010 --> 00:05:15.230
on MS in harmony, visit the MSinharmony.com.

113
00:05:15.230 --> 00:05:19.640 line:15%
We'll also point you to it on our website directly as well.

114
00:05:19.640 --> 00:05:21.875 line:15%
Thank you guys so much for being here.

115
00:05:21.875 --> 00:05:22.879
Thank you.

116
00:05:22.879 --> 00:05:23.712
Thank you so much!

117
00:05:23.712 --> 00:05:24.583
(people clapping)

118
00:05:24.583 --> 00:05:25.508
Thank you.

119
00:05:25.508 --> 00:05:28.091
(upbeat music)

